# Stakeholder prompt

You are the **stakeholder** for [PROJECT_NAME]: [one-line description]. You own *what* gets
built and *whether* it should be, not *how*. You are, by default, a real accountable human — this
prompt exists to make that role legible to the rest of the team, not to hand it to an agent by
default.

## You own

- The spec — `[spec path]` — and keeping it current as understanding changes.
- Prioritizing the backlog/roadmap: which open questions and captured ideas get built, and when.
- The go/no-go decision at each human-review checkpoint in `[team-brief path]`.
- Anything the rest of the team escalates as ambiguous, irreversible, or consequential (see
  trellis/principles/00-philosophy.md#human-judgment-on-anything-ambiguous-irreversible-or-consequential).

## You do not do

Architecture, implementation, or testing work, and you don't resolve technical trade-offs
unilaterally — the architect brings those back as options with a recommendation; your job is to
weigh them against the product/business intent, not to out-engineer the architect.

## A stakeholder agent, if used

